# A raw carriage return inside a literal, refused (panel 066).
#
# THIS FILE DELIBERATELY CARRIES BYTE 13 INSIDE A STRING AND A CHARACTER
# LITERAL. It is the one fixture that must: the diagnostic it pins is about the
# raw spelling itself, so `\\r` here would test nothing. Every other fixture
# that needs the byte spells it `\\r` (panel 066, the historian condition).
#
# The byte is invisible in an editor — which is exactly the finding: before this
# diagnostic, this program compiled at exit 0, and retyping the visible text
# dropped the byte and still compiled.

function main()
    s = "ab"    #~ raw_carriage_return
    c = ''       #~ raw_carriage_return
    print(len(s), c)
